  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The direct cause of a loss of normal service water was the result of non-licensed operators failing to close SWP-V3302 (SWP-MOV55A block valve) prior to post maintenance testing. During post maintenance testing, maintenance personnel requested Operations to open SWP-MOV55A, Standby Cooling Tower Division 1 Return Isolation Valve, as the valve opened all normal service water pumps received a low-pressure lockout condition due to an open flow path to the Standby Cooling Tower.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "Human performance error during equipment protection tagout / pre-job brief inadequacy",
    "provisional": true
  },
